window.GLOSS={};
window.EN={"1":"Grannvale's great army lay waiting for Sigurd, who had quelled the civil war in Silesse.","2":"After subduing Saxony Castle, Sigurd and his group, without even a moment's rest,","3":"found themselves facing the Grannvale army at Lubeck Castle.","4":"Leading that army was Lord Langobalt, one of the men who killed his father.","5":"The battle against Langobalt, who had framed his father Lord Byron,","6":"was also, for Sigurd, a memorial service for his father.","7":"In the desert town of Finora, Lord Arvis's capable retainer,","8":"the sword-mage Vaha, was stationed; and at Vertomer,","9":"General Ide, said to be Arvis's right hand, guarded the castle.","10":"And meanwhile, in the capital, Belhalla,","11":"Lord Arvis supported the aged, bedridden King Azmur,","12":"while Chancellor Reptor handled the nation's public order.","13":"The road to the capital, Belhalla, was long, and a clash with the pursuing army was unavoidable.","14":"They could no longer bear to drag Silesse, who had cared for them, further into this war.","15":"Sigurd and his group resolved on this final battle. In the early spring of the year 760 of the Grannvale calendar,","16":"the mountains and fields of Silesse were still covered in deep snow.","17":"Ugh... Sigurd... I cannot die yet...","18":"Not until I pass this holy sword, Tyrfing, to you...","19":"Lord Langobalt,","20":"we found Lord Byron, who was on the run, but he slipped away from us just as we were closing in.","21":"It seems he intends to flee into Silesse.","22":"What, you fool! Chase him at once!!","23":"We annihilated the holy knights of Sylvail, the Grutia Knights, with our surprise attack,","24":"but if Byron's still alive, it's all for nothing!","25":"Yes sir, but he's suffered considerable wounds, so he shouldn't last much longer...","26":"That's exactly why I say you're too soft.","27":"Byron is mustering his last strength to try to pass the holy sword Tyrfing to his son.","28":"If that sword falls into Sigurd's hands, it'll cause no end of trouble later—don't you see that!","29":"Sortie at once and kill Byron!!","30":"Yes sir, understood.","31":"Damn it, that Dagan still hasn't come with reinforcements.","32":"Leading the elite axe-knight corps, the Grau Ritter, yet unable to suppress even a single rebellion in Isaach...","33":"Both Lex and Dagan, useless sons, the lot of them.","34":"Lord Langobalt, there's no need to worry. As long as I have my Vaegrite, there's nothing to fear from traitors.","35":"I'm grateful, Lord Andrei. When the time comes, lend me your strength.","36":"Heh heh, leave it to me...","37":"Damn it, that insolent brat. He killed his own father and shows not the slightest guilt.","38":"Lord Reign is a pitiful man too...","39":"Lord Sigurd, it seems a lone knight is heading this way from the east.","40":"What? An enemy!?","41":"No, it looks like a pursuit force came out from Lubeck Castle, so I think it's probably an ally.","42":"I see, then we must help him... in any case, a battle with Langobalt's army can't be avoided.","43":"Right, our first battle, where we crush the enemy's front line in one stroke, will decide everything!","44":"Big Sister, is something wrong?","45":"Edain, you've heard about Andrei too, haven't you.","46":"Yes, that he laid hands on Father, and even Lady Mahnya of Silesse...","47":"Has Andrei been possessed by a demon, I wonder?","48":"I will kill Andrei. So that he commits no more sins than this, it must be done.","49":"Edain, you understand, don't you?","50":"Big Sister...","51":"It's painful, but please bear with it. His sin is our sin too.","52":"My hands will be stained with blood, but I want at least you, Edain, to understand.","53":"Yes... Big Sister Brigid...","54":"[Only if Claude and Edain are a couple]","55":"Edain, the final battle is finally here.","56":"Yes, Father Claude...","57":"I'll leave this with you. Use it to help the young soldiers.","58":"This is the Rescue Staff, isn't it. But why...","59":"This is something I haven't told anyone, but I'll tell you, my wife, at least.","60":"Listen carefully. This battle will end in our defeat. All the main figures will die.","61":"Wha...!?","62":"When I heard the god's voice at the Tower of Baldr, even I couldn't believe it.","63":"But this is fate. Of course, I will die too. That's why I'm entrusting this staff to you.","64":"No... that's a lie!! I can't believe something like that!!","65":"Please... please tell me it's a lie...","66":"Edain, there's no need to be sad. Our deaths don't mean everything ends.","67":"It's only natural that living things die and things with form are lost, but it doesn't mean becoming nothing.","68":"They change form into something more complete. You mustn't fear death. You mustn't fear loss.","69":"But, Father Claude...","70":"Even if I die, I will be born again.","71":"Look, already, inside you too, there's a new life... that might be me.","72":"That's why Edain must go on living.","73":"No... Father Claude, that's unfair. Are you telling me to live on alone!?","74":"Edain, I was happy to have met you. Please forgive me...","75":"Father Claude...","76":"Lord Arvis, is it true that Sigurd's men are marching toward Belhalla?","77":"Yes, but there's no need to worry.","78":"Lord Langobalt's corps has already deployed to Lubeck, and subduing the rebel army is only a matter of time now.","79":"But, you know, I still can't believe it.","80":"That Lord Byron assassinated Kurth, and that Sigurd raised a rebellion...","81":"Majesty, still saying such things... Lord Byron, in collusion with Lord Ring of Jungby,","82":"harmed Prince Kurth—both Dukes Reptor and Langobalt witnessed it.","83":"They sought to usurp the royal family, and when the prince learned of it, they even took his life...","84":"Of course, Lord Sigurd too is complicit in the rebellion.","85":"As proof of that, he is harboring the prince of the enemy nation, Isaach.","86":"This is clearly treason against the state.","87":"Prince Kurth is now, to me, also a father-in-law...","88":"For the sake of my beloved wife—Deirdre—too, I cannot forgive the rebel Sigurd.","89":"Should Lord Langobalt happen to be defeated,","90":"my House Vertomer's flame-knight corps, the Loh Ritter, will subdue that rebel army for you to see.","91":"I see... if you say so much, there's nothing for it, I suppose...","92":"Arvis, about Deirdre... *cough cough*...","93":"Grandfather! Are you all right? You mustn't push yourself. Please rest now.","94":"Ah, Deirdre... you are such a kind child.","95":"For an old man like me with little time left, you are my one and only hope.","96":"I don't know when Kurth came to have a daughter like you,","97":"but that you are a direct descendant of the royal house of Belhalla is clear from the mark on your forehead.","98":"Until now, where and how were you living...","99":"I'm sorry, Grandfather... I can't remember anything.","100":"I have no memory of anything at all...","101":"Ah, that was a terrible thing to ask... when it's you who suffers most from it.","102":"The princess... when she was found collapsed outside my castle, she had already lost her memory.","103":"She remembered nothing at all except her own name.","104":"At first I looked after her out of sympathy, but before long I came to love her deeply...","105":"I never imagined she was Prince Kurth's own daughter, and I've done something terribly presumptuous.","106":"When you brought the princess to the palace, saying there was a girl you wanted to marry, I doubted my own eyes.","107":"Call it an intuition only those of the same bloodline would know—and indeed, beneath her circlet was the mark of Naga.","108":"Lord Arvis, do you understand?","109":"Only those of my royal house, descendants of Heim, can take up Naga's holy book and unleash its power.","110":"And that power of Naga alone can oppose the dark god Loptous.","111":"Yes, I am well aware.","112":"You must not let the blood of the god Naga... of the saint Heim, die out. The two of you must have a child soon.","113":"And if a child is born who inherits the power of Naga,","114":"make that child the prince, and have him become King of Grannvale after I am gone.","115":"Until the prince comes of age, Lord Arvis, you shall become regent king and guide the prince rightly.","116":"Understood?... *cough, cough, cough*...","117":"They say Grannvale's great army has marched on Lubeck. Is this the end for Silesse too, I wonder...","118":"Our Silesse had always been a peaceful country.","119":"Just when did the world come to be like this, I wonder...","120":"A child's abilities are passed down from the parents.","121":"In many cases, they say a boy inherits more of his father's power, and a girl more of her mother's.","122":"Langobalt's soldiers have been plundering the villages at will.","123":"Even so, I've managed to hide away a little money.","124":"This is our feelings for you. Please, take it.","125":"They say King Eldigan of Nodion had a child with his late wife.","126":"I hear the name was something like Ares, and he's still three or four years old... how pitiful...","127":"Isaach was conquered by Grannvale, but I hear fighting still continues in the regions.","128":"It's said the people of Isaach are eagerly awaiting Prince Shanan's return.","129":"The Grannvale that loved peace is now completely lost.","130":"The Grannvale army has sent troops to each nation, destroying other countries.","131":"If Prince Kurth were still here, things like this would never have been allowed. Please,","132":"return home as soon as possible and take Grannvale back from those wicked men's hands.","133":"[Only if Ardan has a sweetheart]","134":"...Even someone like me got married and had a child. From now on I have to work hard for my family too—I can't afford to die for a while yet...","135":"Hm? What's this old book? I can't make heads or tails of what it's written...","136":"Hm... mmm...! Wh-what is this feeling! My senses are growing sharper...","137":"Ch... Father, isn't it! Thank goodness! So you're safe!","138":"Sigurd... you've grown so fine... *cough, cough*...","139":"Father! Please, hold on!!","140":"No, I'm already finished. Sigurd, listen well. Prince Kurth was killed by Langobalt.","141":"The one pulling the strings behind it is Reptor. Please tell His Majesty of this.","142":"I... don't mind dying, but I cannot die while branded with the shame of a traitor...","143":"So it really was like that... understood, Father! I will surely clear your disgraced name.","144":"Please, rest easy.","145":"I'm sorry... because I let my guard down, I'm causing you hardship too.","146":"Sigurd, take this. It's the holy sword, Tyrfing...","147":"Tyrfing... but Father, this is still...","148":"Sigurd, I'm counting on you. Avenge my regret, please...","149":"Ah, Father! Please, hold on!! Father...","150":"Lord Sigurd...","151":"What a thing to happen... damn it... Reptor, Langobalt! You two, at least, I will never forgive...","152":"Ugh, so this is the end, is it...","153":"Sigurd... I'm sorry...","154":"[If fought against Byron]","155":"Lord Byron, I'm sorry, but this too is my lord's command. You'll have to die here!","156":"[If fought against any other unit]","157":"What, why are you all here?","158":"Has the front line already been broken through!?","159":"Damn it, I slipped up...","160":"Go! Show them the terror of my Vaegrite in full!!","161":"Fufufu... you fools... die!!","162":"I-impossible... Skasaha... avenge our father for me...","163":"[If fought against Sigurd]","164":"Gahahaha... so you've come, brat. Good timing—I'll send you to join Byron too.","165":"He must be lonely all alone.","166":"Langobalt! You, at least, I will never forgive! Know the depth of my father's regret!","167":"[If fought against Lex]","168":"W-why, you're Lex, aren't you... you traitor! Defying your own father—know shame!!","169":"That's why I said I didn't want to... Old man, this too is fate, forgive me...","170":"[If fought against any other unit]","171":"Gahahaha... small fries, as long as I have this Swanchika axe,","172":"it makes no difference how many of you come—don't come near me if you don't want to die!","173":"I-impossible... that I, of all people, should be defeated... Dagan... I leave the rest to you.","174":"[Only if Byron is alive]","175":"What a thing... Sigurd!! Just one step away... has heaven forsaken me...!","176":"Lord Sigurd, that was a fierce battle.","177":"Indeed, a battle against Grannvale's regular army. From here on it'll get even harder.","178":"So, Oifey, I have a favor to ask of you.","179":"Yes, what is it?","180":"Head northeast from here, Lubeck, and you'll enter Isaach's territory.","181":"Isaach lost its war with Grannvale, and I hear Langobalt's eldest son, Dagan, is now stationed there,","182":"but his reach probably hasn't extended to the outlying regions yet. So...","183":"Please wait! Don't tell me you mean for me to flee to safety!? I don't want that!","184":"I will stay by Lord Sigurd's side to the very end!!","185":"Oifey, you might think I'm being selfish, but please understand.","186":"I don't want to lose Celice. This child isn't even two years old yet. I can't fight while bringing along such a young child...","187":"Oifey, please, I'm begging you, protect Celice.","188":"There's no one I can ask this of but you...","189":"Lord Sigurd... I see... understood.","190":"I will protect Lady Celice even at the cost of my life. But please, make me a promise.","191":"Promise that once this battle ends, you'll surely come for him. Without that promise, I cannot leave.","192":"Understood, I promise. I will surely come for him.","193":"Yes... I believe those words of yours.","194":"Wait! Protecting Celice is my job. I promised Deirdre.","195":"I won't hand him over to Oifey until Deirdre says it's okay!","196":"Shanan... it's all right now...","197":"It seems you're still grieving over Deirdre, but it's fine now, don't worry about it.","198":"No way! I'll protect Celice. The people of Isaach hate Grannvale,","199":"so even if Oifey and the others go, they won't protect him at all.","200":"I'm the prince of Isaach. I can protect Celice. It's... a promise with Deirdre...","201":"Lord Sigurd, I too feel reassured having Shanan with us.","202":"I think you're worried about dragging young Shanan into this,","203":"but he's already a fine warrior. For gaining the cooperation of the people of Isaach too, I think Shanan's strength is needed.","204":"I see...","205":"...I'm sorry, Shanan. I leave Celice to you... please protect him.","206":"Yeah! Leave it to me, I'll get even stronger and protect Celice.","207":"And then, about Deirdre... I'll get Celice to forgive me for it...","208":"Well then, Lord Sigurd, we'll be going. Please stay safe,","209":"and I pray the day of victory comes as soon as possible.","210":"Right, Oifey, take care too.","211":"Yes!","212":"Celice, forgive your father... please... grow up to be fine and strong...","213":"Everyone, just a little more patience, hang in there.","214":"I hear Sigurd's army is heading south through this Yied Desert.","215":"If we head north, we should be able to join up somewhere in the desert.","216":"Quan, I'm truly sorry.","217":"Even though Father is in poor health, he readily agreed to send troops to help my brother.","218":"But, making an enemy of the great nation of Grannvale—when I think of what will become of Leonster's future,","219":"I'm really worried...","220":"Ethlyn, Leonster, small nation though it is, is a house of heroes descended from the Crusader Noba.","221":"If this is a righteous battle, I have no regrets even if we're destroyed—Father told me to fight with an easy heart.","222":"Ethlyn, don't worry. I have this Gae Bolg lance. As long as I have this lance, I will not lose.","223":"I'll surely save Sigurd, you'll see.","224":"Yes, that's right... I'm sure you can...","225":"Ethlyn, it's about time you headed home now. This area is under enemy control, and the fighting could start anytime.","226":"Quan... I thought about it a lot, but, after all, I've decided to come too.","227":"I want to see my brother too, and besides... I don't want to leave your side.","228":"That won't do! You said you'd only see me off partway, so I allowed Altena to come along too.","229":"That's not what we agreed! Altena is only three, and even now she's just sleeping on your lap.","230":"What will you do if fighting breaks out!","231":"Altena won't leave my side even for a moment.","232":"I didn't intend to bring her on this expedition either,","233":"but I couldn't leave her behind crying and screaming.","234":"But you're quite right. Understood, I'll return home.","235":"Ethlyn, I'm sorry. I understand your feelings well, but back home there's also Leaf, who was just born.","236":"The children need their mother. Please wait for my return together with Finn, whom I left to guard the country.","237":"Yes, but just a little longer... just a little, please... let me stay by your side.","238":"Please, Quan...","239":"Ethlyn... understood. Just a little longer, then.","240":"Kukuku... that Quan, bringing a woman along without even knowing we've been tailing him—how carefree.","241":"Leonster's Lance Knights are finished too now.","242":"With their feet caught in the desert sand, they won't be able to fight properly either.","243":"Right, let's go! Thracia's dream is now within our grasp!","244":"What!? Thracia's Dragon Knights! Damn it, we've been tailed by Travant!","245":"Ethlyn!! Run! We cannot fight in the desert!","246":"B-but... dear...","247":"Ethlyn, those men are hyenas. They show no mercy, even to women and children.","248":"Thracia has had its eye on our nation for a long time now.","249":"The reason I entrusted half our forces to Finn and left them behind, even for this expedition, was in preparation for Thracia's movements.","250":"But I never imagined they'd come after us.","251":"This is... my own mistake.","252":"Quan, don't give up, it'll be all right. If we all fight together, we'll manage somehow. Let's hold on to the very end.","253":"Ethlyn... I'm sorry...","254":"Langobalt's dead, has he...","255":"W-what do we do now! Arvis!","256":"Wasn't it you who said Sigurd wasn't worth worrying about!","257":"That's why both Langobalt and I entrusted most of our forces to our sons and sent them to subdue the regions.","258":"This isn't what was promised!","259":"Lord Reptor, there's no need to panic so.","260":"I've already placed my House Vertomer's men on guard in the Yied Desert.","261":"Besides, Thracia's mercenary corps should be arriving soon too. Timing it for when the enemy is tired,","262":"if the duke's corps and mine attack together, we can easily crush Sigurd's rebel army.","263":"Arvis, keep your promise. I don't mind you becoming King of Grannvale after Azmur is gone.","264":"But we too, in turn...","265":"I understand. Once this battle ends, your House Freege will become the royal house of Agustria,","266":"and Lord Langobalt's House Dozel will become the royal house of Isaach. I will surely keep my promise, don't worry.","267":"I see... understood, then I too will fight with all my strength...","268":"Kukuku... Lord Arvis, the plan is proceeding steadily, isn't it.","269":"Manfroy, is it... I've told you many times, but you all must not come out into the open.","270":"Until I gain real power, the shadow of the Loptous Church must not be seen.","271":"Understood. No matter how greedy Reptor and Langobalt may be,","272":"they would never permit our existence alone, would they.","273":"It was the plan all along to use them up and then discard them—after that, we just use their sons instead...","274":"Mm... but Manfroy, I'll say this much at least.","275":"I have no intention whatsoever of rebuilding the Loptous Empire.","276":"I permit your Loptous Church's existence, but I will never entrust the world to the dark god. Don't forget that.","277":"Even if the blood of the Loptous clan flows within my own blood,","278":"that blood is the blood of the holy knight Maira, who fought for the sake of humanity.","279":"As one who inherits the blood of the flame crusader Fala and the holy knight Maira,","280":"I will change this world into one without discrimination, where anyone can live easily.","281":"I feel bad for Sigurd, but he will have to become the sacrifice for that cause.","282":"Ho ho ho... and that too, is for Lady Deirdre's sake, isn't it. Lord Arvis is afraid,","283":"afraid that the queen's memory might return...","284":"Don't say it! Manfroy!! We love each other. I will let no one interfere any longer!","285":"Kukuku... you'd best hurry and have a child.","286":"I'm sure he'll grow up to be a splendid king... kukuku...","287":"So the traitors have come, have they. Kukuku... if they approach, show no mercy—give them a taste of Meteor.","288":"I'll make this desert their graveyard.","289":"[While Ethlyn is alive]","290":"Die! You hyenas!! As long as I have this Gae Bolg, I will not lose to you.","291":"[After Ethlyn has died]","292":"Ugh... so this is the end, is it.","293":"Ethlyn... I'm sorry... Finn, I leave Leaf to you... [Only after Ethlyn has died]","294":"So Quan's dead, has he... good. Magawn, you lead your men and attack Sigurd's army.","295":"There's a high bounty on their heads. Don't let even one of them get away alive.","296":"Yes sir, by the way, what should we do about that child? He won't stop crying and screaming, and everyone's at their wit's end with him.","297":"Should we just kill him quickly and be done with it?","298":"No need for that, hand him over to me. I'll bring him back to Thracia along with the Gae Bolg lance.","299":"That's an unexpected thing to hear... what do you intend to do with him once you bring him back to Thracia?","300":"Fool! That's none of your business!! Don't go sticking your nose into things that don't concern you!!","301":"Yes sir, my apologies. Well then, I'll head out to pursue Sigurd's army.","302":"Mm, I'm counting on you!","303":"Altena, I alone will protect you!","304":"Ah, Altena... forgive me... Quan, I'm sorry... [While Quan is alive]","305":"What? The enemy woman had a child with her... Quan's daughter, is it... this is interesting.","306":"Tell him to throw away the Gae Bolg, or else I'll kill his daughter.","307":"...Heh heh heh, knowing that man, he won't be able to say no.","308":"What! Altena... I see... so Ethlyn is... understood... so this is the end, is it...","309":"I'll throw away the Gae Bolg. So tell them not to lay a hand on my daughter!","310":"[After Quan has died]","311":"What? The enemy woman had a small child with her... Quan's daughter, is it... this is interesting.","312":"Hand him over to me. I'll bring him back to Thracia along with the Gae Bolg lance.","313":"That's an unexpected thing to hear... what do you intend to do with him once you bring him back to Thracia?","314":"Fool! That's none of your business!! Don't go sticking your nose into things that don't concern you!!","315":"Yes sir, my apologies. Well then, I'll head out to pursue Sigurd's army.","316":"Mm, I'm counting on you!","317":"Azel, you don't seem well. What's wrong?","318":"Lex... are you really all right with it?","319":"Hm? ...Ah, about the old man, you mean...","320":"Yeah...","321":"Well... it'd be a lie to say it's nothing, but it can't be helped.","322":"Father killed a great many innocent people. I think it's just deserts.","323":"Lex, you're strong. I'm no good—whenever I think of my brother, my body trembles.","324":"Lord Arvis is a strange man. He was kind to us, and I can't think he's a wicked man at all, so why...","325":"Yeah... to me, he was more than a father.","326":"But sometimes, it was as though he became a different person, and it was frightening... that's why...","327":"That's why you ran away from Lord Arvis's side.","328":"That's fine. Azel, you have your own way of living. Don't worry about it so much.","329":"Yeah... you're right...","330":"Ayra!? Why are you here? I told you to go to Isaach with Shanan and the others.","331":"I'm grateful for the thought, but that wouldn't sit right with me. Sorry, but let me stay to the very end.","332":"Don't be absurd... what good is it if you don't go? You swore to protect Shanan, didn't you.","333":"Yes, because I promised my dead brother...","334":"But Shanan can live a fine life on his own now too. My duty is finished.","335":"But...","336":"I will return to Isaach. Only once this battle is over, though.","337":"And, Lord Sigurd... at that time, you will be with us too.","338":"Jamka...","339":"What, Dew, you're still here? You're done here already, you know. Hurry up and vanish somewhere.","340":"Even you, Jamka, saying something like that. Somehow everyone's acting strange.","341":"Victory should be close, but everyone's on edge. Why is that, I wonder.","342":"Ah, sorry... that's right, I am a bit irritable, come to think of it. I wonder why...","343":"...Jamka, you know, I like you.","344":"I teased you a lot and stuff, but, sorry about that.","345":"Hey now, why bring that up all of a sudden? You're being strange too, Dew.","346":"No, it's just, well... anyway, I'm off, see you around.","347":"Dew is sensing something too...","348":"This is our job too, after all... don't take it personally.","349":"Ugh... glory to Thracia!","350":"Take this, the wrath of heaven! Meteor!!","351":"Ugh... Lord Arvis, forgive me...","352":"We've finally made it to Finora. My homeland is close now.","353":"Oifey and the others... I wonder if Celice is doing well...","354":"Why, Lord Sigurd, welcome.","355":"Ah, you're this town's elder, aren't you. I'm sorry for dragging even such an oasis town into this war.","356":"Mm, it can't be helped... I hear there was a war even to the south of the desert until just a while ago.","357":"What a dangerous world it's become.","358":"A war to the south too... what on earth happened?","359":"From what I hear, Leonster's lance-knight corps was on its way north","360":"when it was attacked by Thracia's Dragon Knights and wiped out entirely.","361":"What!? Is that really true!!","362":"Mm, I hear there was a young lady with the Leonster army too, and everyone's saying what a pity it was.","363":"That's... Ethlyn... Quan, forgive me... forgive me...","364":"All right, now's our chance! Join forces with Vertomer's flame mages and crush the enemy in one stroke!","365":"Good, as planned, let's attack Reptor's corps.","366":"Kill them all. Don't let even one of them live.","367":"What, wh-what did you say! Vertomer has betrayed us!? Damn it... has Arvis plotted against me...","368":"[If fought against Sigurd]","369":"Sigurd!? ...You traitor! Do you intend to defile this sacred ground!","370":"Lord Reptor, it's you who's the traitor!","371":"You must remember framing my father and laying hands on Prince Kurth!","372":"Hmph, fool! Politics is power! Your father died simply because he had no power.","373":"Even you, if you're a knight, should understand that much.","374":"A knight is one who values justice and honor—there's no such thing as justice in your methods.","375":"I have returned to my homeland to restore Grannvale's honor!","376":"Commendable of you, but that's as far as it goes. You too will die as a traitor, same as Byron.","377":"Before my Thoron Hammer, your strength is useless.","378":"Sigurd, know your own powerlessness, wahahaha...","379":"[If fought against Tiltyu]","380":"T-Tiltyu... is it you...","381":"I heard you were with the rebel army, but I never imagined you'd appear before me...","382":"Father... I'm sorry...","383":"Ugh, that Claude! Leading my daughter astray...","384":"It can't be helped... Tiltyu, to protect House Freege's honor, you'll have to die.","385":"! ......Father...","386":"[If fought against Ide]","387":"Ide... you, how dare you betray me...","388":"Ho ho ho... Lord Reptor, you're a poor loser too. It's time to give up now.","389":"[If fought against any other unit] [While hostile to House Vertomer]","390":"Kukuku... know well the terror of the Thoron Hammer!","391":"[While neutral with House Vertomer]","392":"At this point, you're coming with me! Die!!","393":"[While hostile to House Vertomer]","394":"Ugh... impossible...... guh. [While neutral with House Vertomer]","395":"Ugh... that Arvis... just what is he...... guh.","396":"[Only if Ayra and Ardan are a couple]","397":"Ardan, are you all right?","398":"Phew, I'm exhausted. This armor's unbearably heavy.","399":"Heh heh, but it's manly, and I like that about you.","400":"Oh, you say such nice things to me. I like you too, Ayra—you're womanly.","401":"Me, womanly... don't say foolish things.","402":"I can tell, you know. There's no one as adorable as Ayra.","403":"What's wrong, Ardan, do you have a fever or something?","404":"Well, let me say it at least once, at the end. Ayra... I love you.","405":"Wh-what are you... you fool...","406":"[Only if Ayra and Lex are a couple]","407":"Lex, this is finally it, isn't it.","408":"Yeah... but you're a stubborn one too. Won't you go to Isaach no matter what?","409":"Why would I? Because I'm a woman? If that's the reason, I won't forgive even you, Lex. The responsibility for the children should be the same for both of us.","410":"That's true... I'm sorry. It's just, when I think of the children who fled to Isaach...","411":"That's why I'm saying let's go pick them up together. Of course, once this battle is over.","412":"Understood, Ayra, well then, let's go!","413":"Lex... I'm sorry. I only know how to live this one way...","414":"Hahaha, I know that. That's exactly why I love you, Ayra.","415":"I don't know how it'll turn out, but let's go as far as the two of us can together.","416":"Yes...","417":"[Only if Ayra and Horin are a couple]","418":"Horin, this is finally it.","419":"Mm...","420":"There's just one thing I want to ask at the end. Is that all right?","421":"Hm? What is it?","422":"Horin, why do you protect me? There must be some reason.","423":"I've known you since you were little. Protecting you is everything to me.","424":"Huh...!? Horin... don't tell me...","425":"I'm the son of the lord of Sophara, and a fool of a man whose heart was stolen by one beautiful girl...","426":"[Only if Lachesis and Noish are a couple]","427":"Noish, wait!","428":"Lachesis!? You're still here! I told you to go to Leonster.","429":"I sent the children on ahead, but I will fight to the very end.","430":"That's not what we agreed.","431":"The children need their mother. Besides, if something were to happen to you, what would become of Eldigan's child!","432":"Ares is... I don't even know where he is.","433":"Lord Sigurd worried about Prince Ares, who lost both his parents.","434":"To you too, Ares must be special.","435":"No... it's all right now... I am your wife, after all.","436":"Of course, I love you. Don't forget that, at least.","437":"Yes, my dear... I'm sorry.","438":"[Only if Lachesis and Dew are a couple]","439":"Dew, what are you doing in a place like this!","440":"That's not fair—I've gotten a lot stronger too, you know. Give me a little more credit.","441":"I understand. But this coming battle is different from anything so far.","442":"It's too much for you.","443":"Even you, Lachesis, saying something like that. I'm not a child anymore, you know.","444":"Heh heh, I don't think of you as a child. Because...","445":"Huh, Lachesis, you're turning red.","446":"Oh, stop it, Dew!","447":"Lachesis, I had fun. Thanks for being so kind to me.","448":"Dew, me too...","449":"[Only if Lachesis and Beowolf are a couple]","450":"Beowolf...","451":"Lachesis, if anything should happen to me, go to Leonster.","452":"There's Finn and Quan's children in Leonster. Help them in my place.","453":"Don't say such things! When it's time to go, you'll be with me too!","454":"Lachesis, I feel I owe you an apology.","455":"Huh? Why...","456":"I knew how you felt...","457":"! ......","458":"Lachesis, take care. It was a short while, but I had fun.","459":"Wait! Beowolf!!","460":"(This may be a conversation important to Thracia 776.)","461":"[Only if Silvia and Alec are a couple]","462":"Alec, I finally found you.","463":"Silvia? You're still here? No good, hurry back to the castle!","464":"But I'm worried about you, Alec.","465":"Stop talking like a child already. You're a mother now too.","466":"Don't talk about it like it's none of your business. It's your fault, you know.","467":"W-well, that's...","468":"Alec, come back to me. If you're not here, neither I nor Leen can go on living.","469":"Right, please.","470":"Silvia... I know. I'll surely come back...","471":"[Only if Silvia and Levin are a couple]","472":"Hey, Levin...","473":"Hm? What's wrong, Silvia?","474":"Levin, do you like me?","475":"What, all of a sudden!?","476":"Hey, which is it?","477":"I like you—that's why we got together, isn't it.","478":"I see... that's good.","479":"I love you too, Levin, you know... I'll never forget it, you know...","480":"Silvia... you...","481":"[Only if Silvia and Claude are a couple]","482":"Father Claude, are you all right?","483":"Yes, I'm fine. Silvia, you should go now too. You mustn't be with the army.","484":"But...","485":"You mustn't stay by my side any longer than this.","486":"I love you, Father Claude.","487":"That's the same for me too, but...","488":"I won't! I want to stay by your side forever!","489":"That I cannot allow... Silvia, please understand...","490":"[Only if Fury and Noish are a couple]","491":"Ahh, Noish, I finally found you!","492":"Fury, are you all right?","493":"Yes, I'm fine.","494":"I see... good. Fury, don't push yourself too hard. You're not alone anymore, you know.","495":"Yes, but I wonder how the children I left in Silesse are doing. I want to see them soon.","496":"For that very reason, let's hurry and end this war.","497":"Yes, but Noish, please don't push yourself either...","498":"[Only if Fury and Ardan are a couple]","499":"Ardan, are you all right?","500":"I've had it, the desert is the worst!","501":"Heh heh, it'd be nice if you could ride a Pegasus too.","502":"Ah, if only I were about a hundred pounds lighter.","503":"Ardan... please don't die.","504":"Of course not. I finally got a cute wife like you, Fury—there's no way I'd die!","505":"Once this battle's over, let's go to Silesse together. Let's open a little shop, just the two of us.","506":"Yes, it really would be nice if it turned out that way...","507":"[Only if Fury and Levin are a couple]","508":"Lord Levin, this is finally it, isn't it.","509":"Right, but Fury, keep your promise.","510":"Yes, I'll surely come back alive to Silesse—right?","511":"Yeah, I won't die—so you absolutely mustn't die either, Fury!","512":"Yes! I promise.","513":"My dream since I was little has finally come true—I don't want it to end in death in a war!","514":"I will not leave Lord Levin's side.","515":"Mother's waiting in Silesse. She's looking forward to your return even more than mine, Fury.","516":"Yes, Lady Lahna... no, I mean, Mother—I must make her happy...","517":"[Only if Brigid and Alec are a couple]","518":"Alec, Belhalla is close now.","519":"Yeah, I've finally made it back to my homeland.","520":"Can I really return to the country I was born in too... Jungby... I wonder what kind of place it is.","521":"It's a beautiful country, and there are a lot of beautiful women too.","522":"Alec, I won't forgive any cheating!","523":"Hahaha, I know. I don't want to die just yet, after all.","524":"That's right, you mustn't die. You've still got to live on and keep trying for a long time to come.","525":"For the children's sake too, I'll never let you die...","526":"I'll be fine, I'm lucky—I got to make a beauty like you my wife, after all.","527":"Oh, Alec...","528":"[Only if Brigid and Mideel are a couple]","529":"Mideel, are you all right?","530":"Yes, I'm fine. But what about you, Brigid?","531":"I'm fine as long as Mideel is here with me.","532":"I'm happy to have met you, Brigid. I'm grateful.","533":"Why would you say something like that? I don't like it, Mideel, it sounds like some kind of farewell.","534":"I'm sorry, but there's just this one thing I wanted to say...","535":"You liked Edain, didn't you, Mideel. Was it really all right, with me?","536":"I did like Lady Edain, but that wasn't love. The one I loved is only you!","537":"Mideel, thank you... please watch over me to the very end...","538":"[Only if Brigid and Jamka are a couple]","539":"Jamka, are you all right? Not tired?","540":"No, I'm fine. What about you?","541":"I'm fine... because you're here with me...","542":"Honestly, I don't want Brigid to fight. Is it still no good, after all?","543":"What are you saying, it's no good. Jamka, there's no turning back now.","544":"I see...","545":"Jamka... was it really all right, this way?","546":"Hm?","547":"Was it all right, with me? The truth is, you had feelings for Edain...","548":"Brigid! Don't talk nonsense!! I loved you—there's no falsehood in that feeling!!","549":"I-I'm sorry... but... I'm glad I asked...","550":"[Only if Tiltyu and Lex are a couple]","551":"Lex, must you really fight?","552":"Yeah, you should go to Silesse. I'm sure you can live peacefully in that country.","553":"How awful, telling me to go alone...","554":"House Freege will search desperately to bring you back.","555":"But I don't want to hand my child over to either Freege or Dozel. Tiltyu, please understand how I feel!","556":"But...","557":"We were both born under a trivial fate, but","558":"I was happy to meet you at the end, Tiltyu. It was a short while, but I had fun.","559":"Ah, Lex...","560":"[Only if Tiltyu and Azel are a couple]","561":"Azel, don't go!","562":"Tiltyu, it's a promise, right? You go to Silesse. I'll surely follow later too.","563":"But...","564":"You can't fight House Freege. Or do you really think you could kill your own father, Tiltyu!?","565":"That... I couldn't...","566":"That's exactly right. If you were someone who could calmly kill your own father, I couldn't love you.","567":"Tiltyu, I leave the children to you.","568":"Azel!!","569":"[Only if Tiltyu and Claude are a couple]","570":"Father Claude, what should I do...","571":"You can't fight House Freege. It's too much, fighting your own father.","572":"You should go to Silesse. Live peacefully in that country.","573":"But what about you, Father Claude?","574":"I must see this through to the end. That is my duty.","575":"That's so awful! Then what about the children...","576":"I'm sorry to burden you, but please, I'm begging you.","577":"Father Claude!!","578":"[While Reptor is alive]","579":"This is no time to be talking. Please come, Lord Sigurd, after defeating Reptor.","580":"[After Reptor has died]","581":"Why, Lord Sigurd, I'm so glad you're safe.","582":"Just what is the meaning of this? Why is Vertomer helping me?","583":"Lord Arvis knows that you are innocent, Lord Sigurd.","584":"Lord Arvis has said that everything was the scheming of the two dukes, Reptor and Langobalt.","585":"It's just that until now, both dukes' influence was too strong, so even Lord Arvis couldn't act.","586":"I see, that's how it was... that's a relief.","587":"So this means my father's disgraced name can finally be cleared.","588":"Yes, Lord Arvis, together with His Majesty, is waiting in Belhalla for you to come, Lord Sigurd.","589":"Please, come to the capital, Belhalla.","590":"I see, understood, let's go at once.","591":"Lord Arvis should be welcoming you with the entirety of Belhalla's army.","592":"It will surely be a celebration for the whole nation, as your triumphant return, Lord Sigurd.","593":"Thank you. With this, our hard-fought battle finally comes to an end.","594":"At last I can repay the men who fought alongside me too.","595":"Yes...","596":"Lord Sigurd, a triumphant return in broad daylight, how wonderful.","597":"Why, Lord Arvis, thank you for coming all this way to welcome me. By the way, where is His Majesty?","598":"His Majesty is gravely ill, and can no longer even rise from his bed.","599":"Therefore, I am now handling all affairs of state in his place.","600":"I see, that's unfortunate.","601":"Even concerning myself, I caused His Majesty a great deal of distress.","602":"I will go to the palace later and offer my apologies.","603":"There's no need for that.","604":"What?","605":"You will die here as a traitor. An audience with the king is not permitted.","606":"Wh-what... Lord Arvis, what is the meaning of this!","607":"Fufufu... to notice only now—you're too soft, you too.","608":"You conspired with your father, Lord Byron, to usurp the royal house—that fact remains unchanged.","609":"As the husband of Princess Deirdre, I must subdue you, Sigurd. Don't take it personally.","610":"Princess Deirdre!? ...... that's...","611":"I see, you still didn't know. As a parting gift, let me introduce you to my wife.","612":"Deirdre, come here.","613":"Deirdre, this man is Sigurd, the son of Lord Byron, who killed your father. Say a word of resentment to him, at least.","614":"This person is... Lord... Sigurd...","615":"Huh? Deirdre!? ...... don't tell me...","616":"...... why, like that... to me...","617":"Deirdre, that's right! It's you, isn't it!! Ahh...","618":"Do you... know me...","619":"You! You're...!","620":"That's enough now, Deirdre, step back.","621":"This man is dangerous. He must be punished as a traitor.","622":"But... this person is... please, just a little more time to talk...","623":"No. Someone, take the princess somewhere safe!","624":"Wait! Lord Arvis... just a little longer...","625":"Wait, wait!! Deirdre!! Arvis, please! That person is my...","626":"Enough, say no more! All right, I declare to the whole army: capture the traitor Sigurd and his party!","627":"There's no need to keep them alive. Execute them on the spot!!","628":"Arvis! ...You!!","629":"Thus, one era came to an end. The Grannvale upheaval, which began with the expedition to Isaach, led one young man to a strange and fateful destiny, and, along with many sorrowful tales, vanished as fleetingly as it came. Those who fell wounded in the course of the battle: Prince Quan of Leonster, his wife Ethlyn, and the young lord of Sylvail, Sigurd. [Only if there are survivors other than Sigurd, Quan, and Ethlyn] Also, those who stayed with Sigurd to the end but were defeated in the battle at Belhalla, and whose fate remains unknown: [Only if Noish is alive] Knight of Sylvail, Noish. [Only if Alec is alive] Knight of Sylvail, Alec. [Only if Ardan is alive] Great Knight of Sylvail, Ardan. [Only if Lex is alive] Young lord of Dozel, Lex. [Only if Azel is alive] Young lord of Vertomer, Azel. [Only if Ayra is alive] Princess of Isaach, Ayra. [Only if Edain is alive] Young lady of Jungby, Edain. [Only if Mideel is alive] Archer-knight of Jungby, Mideel. [Only if Jamka is alive] Prince of Verdane, Jamka. [Only if Lachesis is alive] Princess of Nodion, Lachesis. [Only if Beowolf is alive] Free Knight, Beowolf. [Only if Horin is alive] Gladiator, Horin. [Only if Dew is alive] Thief, Dew. [Only if Levin is alive] Prince of Silesse, Levin. [Only if Fury is alive] Pegasus Knight of Silesse, Fury. [Only if Silvia is alive] Traveling dancer, Silvia. [Only if Claude is alive] Priest of Edda, Claude. [Only if Tiltyu is alive] Young lady of Freege, Tiltyu. [Only if Brigid is alive] Young lady of Jungby, Brigid. The young ones fought in pursuit of their ideals. But without that dream ever coming true, they fell scattered on the battlefield. Just what, in the end, was their struggle for? And the light is........."};
